the edges it takes, paired with its length. Paths are told apart by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their edges, so parallel edges give distinct paths. Paths of equal length come in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified order. The out-edges and their weights are copied when the sequence is made; each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path after the first then costs up to one shortest-path search per vertex on the path before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. Taking a prefix, ","type":"text"},{"code":"prefix(k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", gives the k shortest simple paths.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each iterator starts over from the first path. Holds a copy of the graph, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPathTree"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The simple paths from a source to a target in order of length, shortest first, listed lazily"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by Yen’s algorithm with Lawler’s refinement."}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestsimplepaths"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ShortestSimplePaths","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0a6SimpleB0V","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestSimplePaths"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestSimplePaths"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ShortestSimplePaths.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths.swift#L326"}},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPat